# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live database dumps. These are full production exports: merchant API keys
# (pk_live_/sk_live_), customer names, emails, phone numbers, bank accounts and
# KYC documents. This repository pushes to GitHub, and a committed secret stays
# in the history for ever even after it is deleted - so they are ignored by
# explicit path rather than by `*.sql`, because real schema files are tracked
# (CODEVAULT/database.sql, EXAM-HUB/install/schema.sql, lm/migrations/*.sql)
# and a wildcard would quietly hide the next one.
/ueozmmmx_vtu.sql
/v8data_vendor.sql
/MERCHANT.PAYHUB/payhubfund_ing.sql
/MERCHANT.PAYHUB/ueozmmmx_vtu.sql

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google/Firebase service-account key. A private key, not a config file: anyone
# holding it can act as that project. Verified NOT to be in this repository's
# history (checked with `git log --all`), so ignoring it from here is enough -
# had it been, the key would have needed rotating instead.
/apps-505118-381f9a756220.json
/service-account*.json

